To implement the slugify function in src/textutil.py, you can use the following code:

```python
import re
from textutil import strip_accents

def slugify(text):
    """
    Convert a string into a URL slug.
    """
    # Convert to lowercase
    text = text.lower()
    
    # Remove accents
    text = strip_accents(text)
    
    # Replace runs of non-alphanumeric characters with a single hyphen
    text = re.sub(r'[-\s]+', '-', text)
    
    # Trim hyphens
    text = re.sub(r'^-+|-+$', '', text)
    
    return text
```

This function first converts the input text to lowercase using the `lower()` method. Then, it removes any accents using the `strip_accents` function from the `textutil` module. Next, it uses a regular expression to replace any runs of non-alphanumeric characters (including spaces and hyphens) with a single hyphen. Finally, it trims any leading or trailing hyphens using another regular expression.

